# Generated-output trees (site/*.html from tools/build-site.js, renders/**/*.svg
# from tools/render-card.js and tools/composite-card-art.js) are written by Node
# with LF line endings. On this Windows machine core.autocrlf=true, so after every
# rebuild git would normalize them back to CRLF on checkout/status, making
# `git status` show phantom modifications even though no real content changed.
# This has aborted automated merges ("local changes would be overwritten") when
# nothing real differed.
#
# Judgment call: pin `* text=auto eol=lf` repo-wide vs. scope it to just the
# generated directories. Scoping was chosen deliberately — it fixes the actual
# problem (noisy diffs on machine-generated files) without touching line-ending
# behavior for hand-authored markdown/JS/JSON elsewhere in the repo, which
# avoids a repo-wide renormalization churning files unrelated to this bug.

# Directory-scoped so any generated file type dropped into these trees in the
# future is covered by default, plus explicit extension rules for the file
# types the generators currently emit (svg, html, and md should one of the
# tools start emitting markdown output).
renders/** text eol=lf
# Raw art images are binary — the text pin above would strip CRLF bytes
# from JPEG data and corrupt them (it did, once).
renders/art-raw/** binary
renders/**/*.svg text eol=lf
renders/**/*.md text eol=lf

site/** text eol=lf
site/**/*.html text eol=lf
site/**/*.md text eol=lf
